---
import FrameworkTabs from '../components/FrameworkTabs.astro';
import Docs from '../layouts/Docs.astro';

const samples = {
  React: `pnpm add @cuttle-ui/react @cuttle-ui/styles

// In your app entry
import '@cuttle-ui/styles';`,
  CLI: `npx @cuttle-ui/cli init
npx @cuttle-ui/cli add button dialog

// In your app entry
import './components/cuttle/cuttle.css';
import { Button } from './components/cuttle';`,
};
---

<Docs title="Installation">
  <p>
    Packages are not published to npm yet. These are the commands that will work from the first
    public release.
  </p>
  <FrameworkTabs samples={samples} />
  <h2>What the CLI does</h2>
  <p>The CLI copies component source into your project, so you own it and can change it.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>cuttle init</code> detects your framework, writes <code>cuttle.json</code> and copies <code>tokens.css</code>.</li>
    <li><code>cuttle add</code> copies components and what they depend on, by default to <code>src/components/cuttle</code>. It adds <code>@cuttle-ui/core</code> to <code>package.json</code>, so run your installer afterwards.</li>
    <li><code>cuttle update</code> brings them up to date with a 3-way merge, which keeps your changes. A clash leaves conflict markers in the file and exits with an error. Use <code>--dry-run</code> to check first.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Commit the <code>.cuttle</code> folder. It holds the versions you started from, which <code>cuttle update</code> needs for merging.</p>
  <p>Vue, Angular, Svelte and Web Components join in later phases.</p>
</Docs>
